{"step_index":528,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T17:07:58Z","content":"Both issues have been identified and resolved:\n\n---\n\n### 1. What Was Causing These Issues & What Was Fixed:\n\n1. **Caller Name Not Transferring to Text Messages:**\n   - The fallback sit-down template in `AiSmsService` had a fallback string before reading your local settings database.\n   - **Fix:** Both the Gemini AI engine and the fallback templates now dynamically retrieve your saved name from Settings and inject it into all messages:\n     > *\"Hi Joseph, this is [Your Name] with ValuTeachers...\"*\n   - `SettingsScreen` now also displays an instant confirmation banner upon saving.\n\n2. **Cannot Delete Contacts or Lists:**\n   - On iOS Safari / mobile web, React Native's `Alert.alert` does not support custom button callback handlers (`onPress`), and the local database needed the explicit SQL handler for `DELETE FROM leads WHERE id = ?`.\n   - **Fix:** Added full cross-platform confirmation dialogs and complete SQLite/local storage delete handlers across `LeadDetailScreen` and `ListsScreen`. Deleting contacts and lists now works instantly on your iPhone.\n\n---\n\n### Push the Fixes to Your Live App (5 Seconds):\n\nIn your PC terminal, run:\n```cmd\nnpx surge ./dist valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh\n```\n*(Replace `valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh` with your exact Surge domain if different).*\n\n---\n\n### To Test on Your Phone:\n1. Open **SnapDialer** on your iPhone.\n2. Go to **Settings**, change your name, and tap **Save** (you will see the green confirmation banner).\n3. Open any contact $\\rightarrow$ tap **Draft Text** $\\rightarrow$ your updated name will be in the message.\n4. Tap **Delete Contact** $\\rightarrow$ confirm $\\rightarrow$ the lead will be removed immediately!"}
